#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1317 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "FRESH, DISCRIMINATING - the four date_not_equal_to decision modes (IsoDateComparison). Row 1: complete DATETIME vs complete date, cores compared at the coarser (day) precision, EQUAL -> != false, clean. Row 2: 2020-06-01 vs partial DTHDTC 2020-05, hulls DISJOINT -> fires. Row 3: 2020-05-10 falls inside the 2020-05 hull, overlap -> clean. Row 4: DTHDTC 'UNKNOWN' passes the not empty guard but has null BOUNDS -- the UNPOSITIONABLE mode. It used to read 'every comparison false, clean'; since H1b (owner ruling 2026-09-17, SPEC 5.2(4) amended, <meta>/plans/SPEC-typed-expression-engine.md) an unbounded hull answers `negate`, so date_not_equal_to FIRES on it in either operand position. That is the right answer here: 'UNKNOWN' is not a date, so DSSTDTC 2020-05-10 is certainly not the same date of death, and the rule now says so. TWO findings: rows 2 and 4."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=002 DSSEQ=1
#expectViolationAt row=4 USUBJID=003 DSSEQ=1
dataset DS class=EVENTS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | DEATH | 2020-05-10T14:30
S1 | DS | 002 | 1 | DEATH | 2020-06-01
S1 | DS | 002 | 2 | DEATH | 2020-05-10
S1 | DS | 003 | 1 | DEATH | 2020-05-10
---

dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DTHDTC  type=Char label="Date/Time of Death"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2020-05-10
S1 | DM | 002 | 2020-05
S1 | DM | 003 | UNKNOWN
---
